<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/95> skos:definition "Geographical area to which the vessel's trip is destined."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/94> skos:definition "Previous port which the vessel has called upon."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/93> skos:definition "Rail station where, according to the transport contract, some chargeable operations must happen (re-weighting, re-fixing of the load, control on equipment and on consignment, etc.)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/92> skos:definition "Indication of a routing place."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/91> skos:definition "The place or location where a document is issued."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/90> skos:definition "Place where one or more special treatments have happened or must happen."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/89> skos:definition "(3105) Place where the registration occurs."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/88> skos:definition "Identification of the location at which the cargo is actually received."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/87> skos:definition "Place/port in the country of destination where the conveyance initially arrives from the \"Last place/port of call of conveyance\" (125)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/86> skos:definition "Country in which the security or guarantee for the movement of goods under a transit procedure is valid."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/85> skos:definition "Place to which the goods are destined."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/84> skos:definition "Place at which the goods are taken over by the carrier according to the contract of carriage."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/83> skos:definition "[3358] Place to which the goods are to be finally delivered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/82> skos:definition "Port of loading at which the cargo is loaded on the pre- carriage vessel used for the transport prior to the main transport."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/81> skos:definition "The fifth optional place or port of discharge as mentioned on the transport document where cargo can be discharged at the option of the shipper."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/80> skos:definition "Place at which the goods are taken over for carriage (operational term), if different from the transport contract place of acceptance (see: 10). Synonym: Place of origin of carriage."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/79> skos:definition "Place or port where final documentation is filed for Customs entry processing."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/78> skos:definition "Port in the country of destination where the conveyance initially arrives from the 'last place/port of call of conveyance' and where a conveyance will be discharging cargoes."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/77> skos:definition "Port in the country of destination where the conveyance initially arrives from the 'last place/port of call of conveyance' and where a conveyance will not be discharging cargoes."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/76> skos:definition "(3099) The port where the goods were first loaded on a vessel."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/75> skos:definition "Only place/location where a transhipment from a means of transport to another means of transport is authorised."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/74> skos:definition "Place/location where a transhipment from a means of transport to another means of transport is not authorised."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/73> skos:definition "A location where bills of lading are released to customers."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/72> skos:definition "The fourth optional place or port of discharge as mentioned on the transport document where cargo can be discharged at the option of the shipper."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/71> skos:definition "A place where cargo is reconsolidated."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/70> skos:definition "The third optional place or port of discharge as mentioned on the transport document where cargo can be discharged at the option of the shipper."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/69> skos:definition "A code to identify the next port of call for a vessel where no cargo will be discharged."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/68> skos:definition "The second optional place or port of discharge as mentioned on the transport document where cargo can be discharged at the option of shipper."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/67> skos:definition "Railway station offering mixed cargo transportation services ."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/66> skos:definition "Railway station offering express transportation services."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/65> skos:definition "Name of the seaport, airport, freight terminal, rail station or other place at which the goods (cargo) are finally (to be) unloaded from the means of transport used for their carriage according to the transport contract."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/64> skos:definition "The first optional place or port of discharge as mentioned on the transport document where cargo can be discharged at the option of the shipper."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/63> skos:definition "A place at which works occur referring to a sub-project."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/62> skos:definition "Port of discharge at which the cargo is discharged from the vessel, used for transport after the main transport (transit port)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/61> skos:definition "(3095) Next port which the vessel is going to call upon."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/60> skos:definition "Place at which the transport means arrives."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/59> skos:definition "To identify the location where the loss occurred."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/58> skos:definition "Identification of the station proceeding to the loading or unloading of a rail wagon on a full track site. (Used only when a rail station is obliged to transfer the load on another wagon for technical reasons - e.g. damage)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/57> skos:definition "Name of the location at which freight and charges for main transport are payable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/56> skos:definition "Last rail station in a predefined section of the chargeable voyage. A complete voyage may be divided in sections, even within one country, that are separately chargeable using different tariff rules (split tariffs)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/55> skos:definition "[3102] Name of a place to which a transport charges tariff applies or where freight and other related charges are to be or have been incurred."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/54> skos:definition "A department within the manufacturing area (e.g. lacquering, assembly)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/53> skos:definition "Place or point from which charges and freight are charged."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/52> skos:definition "Country at which a Customs transit operation is terminated. Synonym: Country of transit termination."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/51> skos:definition "Country in which the security or guarantee for the movement of goods under a transit procedure is not valid."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/50> skos:definition "[3107] To identify the customs office which is responsible for transit formalities en-route."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/49> skos:definition "[3263] Country through which a goods or passengers are routed between the country of original departure and final destination."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/48> skos:definition "Region where item has been or will be produced."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/47> skos:definition "Region known to the consignor or his agent at the time of despatch to be the final region to which the goods are to be delivered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/46> skos:definition "Region from which goods are despatched between countries of a Customs union."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/45> skos:definition "(3086) Customs office at which a transit operation is terminated. Synonym: Customs office of transit termination."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/44> skos:definition "(3410) Place where document is signed or otherwise authenticated. Synonym: Place of issue of document."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/43> skos:definition "Place where Customs undertakes a physical inspection of goods to satisfy themselves that the goods' nature, origin, condition, quantity and value are in accordance with the particulars furnished on the goods declaration (CCC)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/42> skos:definition "[3097] To identify the customs office at which the goods leave or are intended to leave the customs territory of despatch."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/41> skos:definition "[3089] To identify the customs office at which the goods enter the customs territory of destination."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/40> skos:definition "Country where item has been or will be traded."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/39> skos:definition "Country where item has been or will be produced."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/38> skos:definition "[3219] To identify the country where a consignment is off-loaded from the means of transport used for the original exportation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/37> skos:definition "[3331] To identify the country from which goods have been or will be consigned prior to final importation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/36> skos:definition "(3216) Country known to the consignor or his agent at the time of despatch to be the final country to which the goods are to be delivered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/35> skos:definition "[3220] Country from which the goods were initially exported to the importing country without any commercial transaction taking place in intermediate countries. Synonym: Country whence consigned. Country of despatch: Country from which goods are despatched between countries of a Customs union."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/34> skos:definition "[3322] Place at which the cargo is loaded on a means of transport according to the transport contract. The goods may or may not be loaded on the main means of transport at this place or port."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/33> skos:definition "[3356] Place at which the cargo is discharged or unloaded from a means of transport according to the transport contract. The goods may or may not be discharged from the main means of transport at this place or port."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/32> skos:definition "First rail station in a predefined section of the chargeable voyage. A complete voyage may be divided in sections, even within one country, that are separately chargeable using different tariff rules (split tariffs)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/31> skos:definition "A building or part thereof relevant to a particular consignment or transaction."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/30> skos:definition "Country in which raw material or components were originally produced prior to manufacture or assembly in another country."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/29> skos:definition "Name or identification of a railway station/yard relevant to a particular consignment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/28> skos:definition "Country to which the goods are to be delivered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/27> skos:definition "[3239] To identify the country in which the goods have been produced or manufactured, according to criteria laid down for the application of the Customs tariff or quantitative restrictions, or any measure related to trade."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/26> skos:definition "City or town relevant for a particular transaction or consignment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/25> skos:definition "Country relevant for a particular transaction."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/24> skos:definition "Port where final documentation is filed for Customs Entry processing."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/23> skos:definition "Port where goods are released from Customs custody."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/22> skos:definition "[3080] Place at which Customs clearance should or has taken place."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/21> skos:definition "Place of departure, shipment or destination as specified in the terms of sale agreed between the parties."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/20> skos:definition "Place where goods will ultimately be delivered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/19> skos:definition "Factory/plant relevant for a particular consignment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/18> skos:definition "[3156] Warehouse where a particular consignment is to be or has been stored."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/17> skos:definition "Place where goods are transported across a country border."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/16> skos:definition "Place where the ownership of the goods is transferred."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/1> skos:definition "(3018) Point or port of departure, shipment or destination, as required under the applicable terms of delivery, e.g. Incoterms."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/2> skos:definition "[3109] To identify the place where the payment has been or should be made."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/3> skos:definition "Place where equipment tare has been or must be checked for official assessment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/4> skos:definition "[3160] Place at which the goods have been received."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/5> skos:definition "(3214) Port, airport or other location from which a means of transport or transport equipment is scheduled to depart or has departed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/6> skos:definition "A bed in a ward."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/7> skos:definition "(3246) Place to which the goods are to be finally delivered under transport contract terms (operational term)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/8> skos:definition "(3258) Port, airport or other location to which a means of transport or transport equipment is destined."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/9> skos:definition "[3334] Seaport, airport, freight terminal, rail station or other place at which the goods (cargo) are loaded on to the means of transport being used for their carriage."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/10> skos:definition "[3348] Place where the goods are taken over by the carrier."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/11> skos:definition "[3392] Seaport, airport, freight terminal, rail station or other place at which goods are unloaded from the means of transport having been used for their carriage."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/12> skos:definition "Port at which the goods are discharged from the vessel used for their transport."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/13> skos:definition "[3424] Place where goods are to be or have been transferred from one means of transport to another during the course of one transport operation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/14> skos:definition "[3385] To identify the place where a goods item is located."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/location/function/15> skos:definition "Place where the responsibility is transferred."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/156> skos:definition "The object or item is sold."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/157> skos:definition "The object or item is damaged."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/158> skos:definition "The object or item is destroyed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/159> skos:definition "The object or item is conformant."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/160> skos:definition "The object or item is non conformant."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/161> skos:definition "The object or item is dispensed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/162> skos:definition "The object or item is partially dispensed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/status/status/163> skos:definition "The object or item is disposed."@en .
